COMMENT '# Every step kind that has an AWS backend, against a remote environment (written for the real estate: `terraform/aws` with run_services).'
EOL '\n'
COMMENT '# Nothing names a prefix or an address: queues, table, bus, functions, parameters, log groups and the services' addresses come from the'
EOL '\n'
COMMENT '# environment's targets, plus three this file needs: `queue/probe` (the URL of a queue the file creates and deletes itself; a URL, so that'
EOL '\n'
COMMENT '# the confirmations of the steps that use it can be issued before the queue exists), `queue/probe-name` (its name) and `parameter/probe`'
EOL '\n'
COMMENT '# (a parameter it puts and deletes). On a writable environment every mutating step needs its confirmation:'
EOL '\n'
COMMENT '#   dlb run estate/scenarios/remote-kinds.scn --env E --steps <the mutating ones>   (prints the tokens)'
EOL '\n'
COMMENT '#   dlb run ... --continue --confirm T1,T2,...                                       (the whole file, approved)'
EOL '\n'
DIR_MARK '#'
WHITE_SPACE ' '
DIR_NAME '@env'
WHITE_SPACE ' '
DIR_VALUE 'local'
EOL '\n'
DIR_MARK '#'
WHITE_SPACE ' '
DIR_NAME '@var'
WHITE_SPACE ' '
DIR_VALUE 'corr = '
VARIABLE '{{correlation}}'
EOL '\n'
DIR_MARK '#'
WHITE_SPACE ' '
DIR_NAME '@var'
WHITE_SPACE ' '
DIR_VALUE 'msg = kinds-'
VARIABLE '{{uuid}}'
EOL '\n'
DIR_MARK '#'
WHITE_SPACE ' '
DIR_NAME '@var'
WHITE_SPACE ' '
DIR_VALUE 'wait = '
VARIABLE '{{timing/logs}}'
EOL '\n'
EOL '\n'
